1
00:00:00,097 --> 00:00:03,687
(Sheldon:)Of course I understand. And who
are you to tell me about outer space?

2
00:00:03,851 --> 00:00:06,391
Well, I'm the astrophysicist.
"Astro" means "space."

3
00:00:07,396 --> 00:00:09,606
"Astro" means "star."

4
00:00:10,316 --> 00:00:12,986
(Raj:)Let me just tell you,
if we were having this argument...

5
00:00:13,152 --> 00:00:16,192
(Raj:)...in my native language,
I'd be kicking your butt.

6
00:00:16,614 --> 00:00:19,704
(Sheldon:)English is your native language.

7
00:00:20,868 --> 00:00:24,208
(Raj:)Okay, you got me there.
But you're wrong about this.

8
00:00:24,371 --> 00:00:26,661
There's a fine line
between wrong and visionary.

9
00:00:26,832 --> 00:00:29,752
(Sheldon:)Unfortunately,
you have to be a visionary to see it.

10
00:00:29,919 --> 00:00:34,259
(Raj:)God, you think that every thought that
comes out of your head is pure gold.

11
00:00:34,423 --> 00:00:37,173
(Raj:)Let me tell you,
some of those thoughts are pure caca.

12
00:00:37,343 --> 00:00:38,923
(Sheldon:)Caca?

13
00:00:39,136 --> 00:00:41,926
-It means "doo-doo."
-All right.

14
00:00:42,098 --> 00:00:45,268
(Sheldon:)First of all, Dr. Koothrappali, when I first
proposed that you work with me--

15
00:00:45,434 --> 00:00:47,264
Aha! So I am working with you?

16
00:00:47,436 --> 00:00:49,146
(Sheldon:)In this context,
"with me" means "for me."

17
00:00:49,313 --> 00:00:51,523
Oh. Yeah, well, in this context:

18
00:00:51,690 --> 00:00:52,730
[BLOWS RASPBERRY]

19
00:00:52,900 --> 00:00:54,530
(Howard:)All right.

20
00:00:54,693 --> 00:00:56,403
(Sheldon:)If I'm wrong, prove it.

21
00:00:56,570 --> 00:00:57,610
(Penny:)Okay.

